  '[{"key":"A","text":"$x = 2$ and $x = 3$"},{"key":"B","text":"$x = -2$ and $x = -3$"},{"key":"C","text":"$x = 1$ and $x = 6$"},{"key":"D","text":"$x = -1$ and $x = -6$"}]'::jsonb,
  'A', NULL,
  E'The correct answer is A. Factor the quadratic: $x^2 - 5x + 6 = (x - 2)(x - 3) = 0$. Setting each factor equal to zero gives $x = 2$ or $x = 3$. Choice B has the correct absolute values but wrong signs. Choice C uses a factor pair of $6$ that does not sum to $-5$.',
  '{"A":{"role":"correct","error_taxonomy":null},"B":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"sign_error"},"C":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"equation_setup_error"},"D":{"role":"distractor","error_taxonomy":"sign_error"}}'::jsonb,
  NULL, 'draft', 1, 45, false,
  '{"provenance":"Lyceon original","authored_by":"claude","authored_date":"2026-07-01"}'::jsonb,
  '{"model":"claude","generation_date":"2026-07-01","prompt_version":"questions_governance_v1"}'::jsonb
);

-- Q25: Math Grid-in Medium — Advanced Math / Nonlinear Equations in One Variable and Systems of Equations in Two Variables
INSERT INTO questions (id, section, source_type, domain, skill_codes, difficulty, item_type, stem, passage, options, correct_answer, correct_variants, explanation, option_metadata, assets, status, version, estimated_time_seconds, premium_flag, source_lineage, generation_attribution)
VALUES (
  'SATM2ZKWMR6', 'M', 2, 'Advanced Math', ARRAY['Nonlinear Equations in One Variable and Systems of Equations in Two Variables'], 2, 'grid_in',
